{"records":[{"id":"xs39gcwsdc","title":"Evaluation of Machine Learning Models and SHAP Visualization on the Diagnosis of Triple Negative and Non-Triple Negative Breast Cancer","description":"Data and codes for triple negative breast cancer and non triple negative breast cancer.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-05-16T14:28:00.203Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xs39gcwsdc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xs39gcwsdc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liyang","last_name":"Su","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"the Joint funds for the innovation of science and technology, Fujian province","grant_id":"2023Y9231"},{"id":null,"name":"the Startup Fund for scientific research, Fujian Medical University","grant_id":"2023QH1300"},{"id":null,"name":"Quanzhou Science and Technology Project","grant_id":"2023NS043"}],"categories":["Breast Cancer","Ultrasound"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zdmthbkcgj","title":"Ferrucci et al., 2020. Prune-1 drives polarization of tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) within the lung metastatic niche in triple negative breast cancer. iSCIENCE-D-20-01279. FiguresHigherResolution","description":"Prune-1 drives polarization of tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) within the lung metastatic niche in triple-negative breast cancer\nVeronica Ferrucci et al., iSCIENCE-D-20-01279. \n\nAbstract:  M2 tumor-associated macrophages (M2-TAMs) in the tumor microenvironment represent a prognostic indicator for poor outcome in triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC). Here we show that Prune-1 overexpression in human TNBC patients has positive correlation to lung metastasis and infiltrating M2-TAMs. Thus, we demonstrate that Prune-1 promotes lung metastasis in a genetically engineered mouse model of metastatic TNBC augmenting M2-polarization of TAMs within the tumor microenvironment. Thus, this occurs through TGF-β enhancement, IL-17F secretion and extracellular vesicle protein content modulation. We also find murine inactivating gene variants in human TNBC patient cohorts that are involved in activation of the innate immune response, cell adhesion, apoptotic pathways, and DNA\nrepair. Altogether we indicate that the overexpression of Prune-1, IL-10, COL4A1, ILR1, and PDGFB, together with inactivating mutations of PDE9A, CD244, Sirpb1b, SV140, Iqca1, and PIP5K1B genes, might represent a route of metastatic lung dissemination which need future prognostic validations.\n\nBelow are Figures of the manuscript in Higher Resoltion","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-12-11T16:32:13.786Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zdmthbkcgj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zdmthbkcgj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Massimo","last_name":"Zollo","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genetics","Breast Cancer","Animal Biomedical Model"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"477bs297n5","title":"A Study of PKCα-mediated nuclear translocation of cGAS stabilizes β-catenin and drives metastasis. Qimin Zhang et al","description":"Although recent studies have shown that 2′3′-cyclic GMP-AMP synthase (cGAS) has both canonical cytoplasmic and noncanonical nuclear functions, the role of nuclear cGAS in cancer metastasis remains unclear. Here, we identify a STING-independent mechanism by which nuclear cGAS activates Wnt/β-catenin signaling to promote metastatic dissemination in triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC). Cytosolic protein kinase C alpha (PKCα) phosphorylates cGAS at Ser120, facilitating its nuclear translocation. Once in the nucleus, cGAS disrupts the interaction between β-catenin and tripartite motif-containing protein 33 (TRIM33), an E3 ubiquitin ligase, thereby preventing β-catenin ubiquitination and promoting its stabilization. This, in turn, activates Wnt/β-catenin signaling. PKCα thus acts as a key regulator of this non-canonical, cGAS-driven metastatic pathway. Therapeutic TAT peptides designed to inhibit cGAS phosphorylation significantly reduce metastatic dissemination. Clinically, elevated nuclear cGAS expression is associated with increased metastasis in TNBC cohorts. Together, these findings delineate a PKCα–cGAS–TRIM33 axis that regulates nuclear β-catenin stability and establish cGAS phosphorylation as a promising theragnostic target for TNBC metastasis.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-22T09:35:51.176Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/477bs297n5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/477bs297n5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Qimin","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"82172823, 32450566, and 81901621"},{"id":"https://ror.org/04323m874","name":"Science and Technology Department of Sichuan Province","grant_id":"2024NSFJQ0047"},{"id":"https://ror.org/0426zh255","name":"China Postdoctoral Science Foundation","grant_id":"2019M652624"}],"categories":["Metastasis","Ubiquitylation","Triple-Negative Breast Cancer","cGAS-STING Signaling Pathway"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6ymdpxmjrt","title":"Carcinoma en Cuirasse is an Independent Poor Survival Predictor in Breast Carcinoma Patients with Cutaneous Metastasis","description":"This supplemental file accompanies our manuscript on the clinical characteristics and prognostic factors of breast cancer patients presenting with cutaneous metastasis. It contains detailed additional figures and tables to support and expand upon the analyses presented in the main article.\n\nSupplemental Figure 1: \nKaplan-Meier curves depicting significant differences in overall survival (OS) among breast cancer patients stratified by metastatic involvement. Patients are categorized into three groups: (1) cutaneous metastasis only (best prognosis), (2) cutaneous plus lymph node metastasis (intermediate prognosis), and (3) cutaneous plus distant metastasis (worst prognosis). Differences between groups were statistically significant.\n\nSupplemental Figure 2: \nMultivariable stepwise selection analyses evaluating clinicopathological features affecting overall survival (OS) and cutaneous metastasis-free survival (CMFS). Both forward and backward stepwise regression methods were employed to construct a robust final predictive model (global model significance: p-value < 0.0001, log-rank test).\n\nSupplemental Figure 3: \nResults from the multivariable stepwise selection analysis specifically modeling clinicopathological predictors of cutaneous metastasis-free survival (CMFS) in breast cancer patients presenting with skin metastasis.\n\nSupplemental Table 1: \nClinicopathological details of 11 breast cancer patients specifically presenting with carcinoma en cuirasse. Data include patient demographics (age), clinical descriptions of skin lesions, duration of lesion presence, histological confirmation of breast carcinoma, and receptor status of cutaneous metastasis (Luminal A, Luminal B HER2-negative, Triple Negative, or unavailable).\n\nSupplemental Table 2: \nMultivariable Cox regression analysis identifying key prognostic factors significantly associated with cutaneous metastasis-specific survival (CMSS). The table details hazard ratios, 95% confidence intervals, and corresponding p-values. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-04-25T09:52:48.419Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6ymdpxmjrt","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6ymdpxmjrt"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ryan","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sophia","last_name":"Shalhout","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Andrew","last_name":"Gerber","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Amy","last_name":"Ly","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mai","last_name":"Hoang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology","Dermatopathology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3vtwfjh2sb","title":"Enhanced SREBP2-driven cholesterol biosynthesis by PKCl/i  deficiency in epithelial intestinal cells promotes aggressive serrated tumorigenesis ","description":"The metabolic and signaling pathways regulating aggressive mesenchymal colorectal cancer (CRC) initiation and progression through the serrated route are largely unknown. Although relatively well characterized as BRAF mutant cancers, their poor response to current targeted therapy, difficult preneoplastic detection, and challenging endoscopic resection makes the identification of their metabolic requirements a priority. Here we demonstrate that the phosphorylation of SCAP by the atypical PKC (aPKC), PKC/ promotes its degradation and inhibits the processing and activation of SREBP2, the master regulator of cholesterol biosynthesis. We show that the upregulation of SREBP2 and cholesterol by reduced aPKC levels is essential for controlling metaplasia and generating the most aggressive cell subpopulation in serrated tumors in mice and humans. Since these alterations are also detected prior to neoplastic transformation, together with the sensitivity of these tumors to cholesterol metabolism inhibitors, our data indicate that targeting cholesterol biosynthesis is a potential mechanism for serrated chemoprevention.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-11-07T07:23:58.1Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3vtwfjh2sb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3vtwfjh2sb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Moscat","last_name":"Diaz-Meco","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cholesterol","Colorectal Cancer","Therapeutics","Cholesterol Metabolism"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"6jbv72m5zv","title":"Proteomic Data of Hedyosmum brasiliense Essential Oil Against Breast Cancer Cells","description":"This dataset contains raw proteomic data derived from label-free quantitative mass spectrometry (shotgun proteomics) of human breast epithelial cells (MCF-10A) and triple-negative breast cancer cells (MDA-MB-231), either untreated or treated with Hedyosmum brasiliense essential oil. Data are provided in Excel format and include protein identifiers, quantification values, fold changes, and statistical significance (p-values). The files are organized by cell type comparison:\n\nPTN_TABLE_HB10A x CTRL10A.xlsx – Proteomic data comparing treated and control MCF-10A cells\n\nPTN_TABLE_HBMDA x CTRLMDA.xlsx – Proteomic data comparing treated and control MDA-MB-231 cells\n\nThese data support the manuscript: Hedyosmum brasiliense Essential Oil Induces Necrotic Cell Death in Triple-Negative Breast Cancer via Tubulin Destabilization and Stress Pathway Dysregulation.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-07-24T15:20:45.194Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/6jbv72m5zv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/6jbv72m5zv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Fabiana","last_name":"Barcelos Furtado","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Geysson Javier ","last_name":"Fernandez","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","grant_id":"2015/14278-6"}],"categories":["Proteomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ch24bpf65r","title":"legacy12159_breast_cancer","description":"Breast cancer cohort from the Phase 1b trial (NCT01623349). Eligible patients had recurrent triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC), or recurrent breast cancer of any subtype with a germline BRCA mutation and were enrolled to a dose escalation or expansion cohort.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-01-10T17:15:23.679Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ch24bpf65r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ch24bpf65r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Felipe","last_name":"Batalini","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gerburg","last_name":"Wulf","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Clinical Research"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b6555hx877","title":"PRRX2-Mediated Transcriptional Regulation of GLI2 Promotes Cell Proliferation, Invasion and Metastasis by Suppressing Cellular Senescence via Hedgehog Signaling in Pancreatic Cancer","description":"PRRX2-Mediated Transcriptional Regulation of GLI2 Promotes Cell Proliferation, Invasion and Metastasis by Suppressing Cellular Senescence via Hedgehog Signaling in Pancreatic Cancer","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-08-09T17:36:12.14Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b6555hx877","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b6555hx877"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jianxin","last_name":"Jiang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Cancer Cell"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f9wgj84d7z","title":"Alterations of Ceramide Synthesis Induce PD-L1 Internalization and Signaling to Regulate Tumor Metastasis and Immunotherapy Response. Wofford et al.","description":"Raw WB images.\n\nProgrammed death-ligand 1, PD-L1 (CD274) facilitates immune evasion and exerts pro-survival functions in cancer cells. Here, we report a new mechanism whereby internalization of PD-L1 in response to alterations of bioactive lipid/ceramide metabolism by ceramide synthase 4 (CerS4) induces sonic-hedgehog (Shh) and TGF- receptor signaling to enhance tumor metastasis in triple-negative breast cancers (TNBC), exhibiting immunotherapy resistance. Mechanistically, data showed that internalized PD-L1 interacts with an RNA-binding protein Caprin-1 to stabilize Shh/TGFBR1/Wnt mRNAs to induce -catenin signaling and TNBC growth/metastasis, consistent with increased infiltration of FoxP3+ T regs and resistance to immunotherapy. While mammary tumors developed in MMTV-PyMT/CerS4-/- were highly metastatic, targeting the Shh/PD-L1 axis using Sonidegib and anti-PD-L1 antibody vastly decreased tumor growth and metastasis, consistent with the inhibition of PD-L1 internalization and Shh/Wnt signaling, restoring anti-tumor immune response. These data, validated in clinical samples and databases, provide a mechanism-based therapeutic strategy to improve immunotherapy responses in metastatic TNBCs. ","source":{"id":"061ffc66-7e7e-46e8-80ac-358a4283c3fe","name":"Medical University of South Carolina","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-05-15T07:31:34.168Z","url":"https://musc.digitalcommonsdata.com/datasets/f9wgj84d7z","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f9wgj84d7z"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Wyatt","last_name":"Wofford","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Ceramide","Metastasis","Western Blot","Programmed Death-Ligand 1"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"bbz8353xwh","title":"NMR-based Metabolomics Analysis Predict Response to Neoadjuvant Chemotherapy for Triple Negative Breast Cancer","description":"Raw data of the \"NMR-based Metabolomics Analysis Predict Response to Neoadjuvant Chemotherapy for Triple Negative Breast Cancer\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-05T06:30:33.121Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bbz8353xwh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bbz8353xwh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jinping","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Nuclear Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":135154,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":107,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":135154,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":134492,"restricted":70,"embargoed":592},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2295},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":693},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":474},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":429},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":424},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":413},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":398},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":317},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":279},{"id":"https://ror.org/05r0vyz12","name":"Ministerio de Ciencia, Innovación y Universidades","count":228}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":132513},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1904},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":183},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":138},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":74},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":65},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":56},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":42},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":32},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":27}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":511},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":407},{"id":"f58d7a83-6efa-5d8a-a6c2-b9e78ee14783","name":"Maharishi Markandeshwar Institute of Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation","count":360},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":359},{"id":"48c8fa0f-965c-5cbf-a859-a5363432478b","name":"Universidade de Sao Paulo","count":305}]}}